# 低频词汇 List06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List06核心词汇

{{contend}}{/kənˈtend/}{竞争；主张}{Several candidates contended for the leadership position.}}
{{convict}}{/kənˈvɪkt/}{定罪；罪犯}{The jury convicted the man of embezzlement.}}
{{copyright}}{/ˈkɒpɪraɪt/}{版权；著作权}{The content is protected under copyright law.}}
{{correspond}}{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/}{通信；对应}{The data corresponds with the published statistics.}}
{{corridor}}{/ˈkɒrɪdɔːr/}{走廊；通道}{The offices are connected by a long, narrow corridor.}}
{{costume}}{/ˈkɒstjuːm/}{服装；戏装}{The actors wore elaborate costumes for the period drama.}}
{{counter}}{/ˈkaʊntər/}{柜台；反击}{The government took measures to counter the economic slowdown.}}
{{coupon}}{/ˈkuːpɒn/}{优惠券；息票}{Customers can redeem coupons for discounts on their next purchase.}}
{{courtesy}}{/ˈkɜːtəsi/}{礼貌；好意}{As a courtesy, please silence your phones during the performance.}}
{{coverage}}{/ˈkʌvərɪdʒ/}{报道；覆盖范围}{The event received extensive media coverage.}}
{{crack}}{/kræk/}{裂缝；破裂}{A crack in the foundation needs immediate repair.}}
{{credential}}{/krɪˈdenʃl/}{资格证书；资质}{The program requires specific academic credentials.}}
{{critique}}{/krɪˈtiːk/}{评论；批评}{The reviewer offered a balanced critique of the novel.}}
{{crude}}{/kruːd/}{粗糙的；原油}{The country is one of the world's largest crude oil exporters.}}
{{crush}}{/krʌʃ/}{压碎；镇压}{The hydraulic press can crush metal objects with ease.}}
{{crystal}}{/ˈkrɪstl/}{水晶；晶体}{The chandelier was made of hand-cut crystal.}}
{{cuisine}}{/kwɪˈziːn/}{烹饪；菜肴}{The restaurant is known for its fusion cuisine.}}
{{cult}}{/kʌlt/}{崇拜；邪教}{The cult attracted followers with its charismatic leader.}}
{{cumulative}}{/ˈkjuːmjələtɪv/}{累积的；渐增的}{The cumulative effect of the reforms was significant.}}
{{curb}}{/kɜːb/}{抑制；路缘}{New regulations aim to curb excessive speculation.}}
{{custody}}{/ˈkʌstədi/}{监护；拘留}{The father was awarded joint custody of the children.}}
{{cynical}}{/ˈsɪnɪkl/}{愤世嫉俗的；怀疑的}{Years of disappointment made him cynical about politics.}}
{{dawn}}{/dɔːn/}{黎明；开端}{The dawn of the internet age changed everything.}}
{{deadline}}{/ˈdedlaɪn/}{截止日期}{The deadline for applications is the end of this month.}}
{{decay}}{/dɪˈkeɪ/}{腐烂；衰退}{Urban decay has affected many inner-city neighborhoods.}}
{{deceive}}{/dɪˈsiːv/}{欺骗；蒙蔽}{The company tried to deceive regulators with false reports.}}
{{decisive}}{/dɪˈsaɪsɪv/}{决定性的；果断的}{Her decisive leadership guided the organization through the crisis.}}
{{declaration}}{/ˌdekləˈreɪʃn/}{宣言；声明}{The declaration outlined the rights of all citizens.}}
{{deduce}}{/dɪˈdjuːs/}{推断；演绎}{From the clues, the detective deduced the identity of the thief.}}
{{deem}}{/diːm/}{认为；视为}{The court deemed the evidence admissible.}}
